{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And you shall not covet.</b> Coveting is only in the heart. If he resolves in his heart — by entreaties, or by multiplying friends, or by intimidation — that he sell him his object, he immediately transgresses 'you shall not covet.' If he expresses his desire verbally, he transgresses 'you shall not covet' — all of them have 'and not,' 'and not,' except 'you shall not murder,' which has no vav. From 'Anokhi' until 'and to those who keep My commandments,' there is between the first Decalogue and the second no change at all, because the Holy One, blessed be He, repeated and expounded them exactly as they are expounded in the section of Yitro, and Moses did not wish to change anything in them even in this section. But as for the rest, which Moses repeated and expounded, there is no concern about a change in wording since they are equal in meaning. And this is the rule: any matter where there is a change in Scripture, you will find the second time different words but the meaning the same; and as for 'You shall not steal,' in which there is no change, there is no need to be strict, for so the verse was. And the Ten Commandments in the section of Yitro are the words of the Holy One, blessed be He, without addition or subtraction — except for 'that it may go well with you,' as Rashi explained — and they alone are what is written on the tablets of the covenant. And those in this section are the words of Moses. Here Moses ordered them according to the reasoning of young men, who first covet a woman, afterward a house, afterward a slave and maidservant, afterward fields and donkeys. And in the section of Yitro the Holy One, blessed be He, ordered them according to the reasoning of wise men, who first acquire a house, afterward a woman, afterward a slave and maidservant, afterward an ox and a donkey."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {0 "פירש״י resolved as 'Rashi explained' per the compiler's convention of citing Rashi without his Hebrew name spelled out; the abbreviation stands for פירש רש״י."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:51:55.089631667Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}